.\autonomous\99_total\PROMPT_guideline.md:100:- benchmark and replay program doctrine
.\autonomous\99_total\PROMPT_guideline.md:229:When the stack is being compared, promoted, benchmarked, or adapted:
.\autonomous\99_total\PROMPT_guideline.md:231:- benchmark, replay, critique, adaptation, and route-quality surfaces should stay separately reviewable when they drive different decisions
.\autonomous\99_total\PROMPT_guideline.md:234:- packet families such as `Benchmark registry memo`, `Context sufficiency review memo`, `Critique quality review memo`, `Adaptation promotion review memo`, `Route-quality scorecard`, and `Coding benchmark scenario memo` should stay lookup-visible when those surfaces are active
.\autonomous\99_total\PROMPT_guideline.md:236:- operational packets such as `Benchmark cohort manifest`, `Replay runner verdict sheet`, `Context substrate scorecard`, `Critique delta ledger`, `Adaptation controller audit packet`, `Route-switch benchmark verdict`, `Coding benchmark execution ledger`, `Release promotion decision record`, and `Telemetry drift investigation memo` should become visible when linked execution evidence, controller behavior, or decision-grade auditability is the active control issue
.\autonomous\99_total\PROMPT_guideline.md:247:- shared execution identifiers such as `scenario_id`, `run_id`, `cohort_id`, `trace_id`, and `artifact_version` should remain stable whenever benchmark, replay, adaptation, release, and telemetry evidence must be linked across rounds
.\autonomous\99_total\PROMPT_guideline.md:253:- benchmark-grade, replay-grade, controller-grade, coding-proof-grade, release-grade, drift-grade, route-quality-grade, and retrieval-substrate-grade language should not outrun `Benchmark cohort manifest`, `Replay runner verdict sheet`, `Adaptation controller audit packet`, `Coding benchmark execution ledger`, `Release promotion decision record`, `Telemetry drift investigation memo`, `Route-switch benchmark verdict`, and `Context substrate scorecard`
.\autonomous\99_total\PROMPT_guideline.md:475:- benchmark and evalset design
