"qualitative_findings":["This is the baseline slice across BE-SHARED-001, BE-SHARED-006, BE-SHARED-011, BE-SHARED-016, and BE-CODEX-001.","All five cases have explicit support in the archived actor outputs and no observed forbidden behavior.","The evidence remains read-only benchmark evidence, not production or stable-v36 proof."],"conclusion":"Baseline is clean in this read-only slice; no component removal signal is needed."},{"variant_id":"remove_clean_state_checklist","removed_component":"lifecycle/clean-state-checklist.md","cases_executed":5,"pass":4,"partial":1,"fail":0,"not_evaluated":0,"state_failures":0,"verification_failures":0,"scope_creep_count":0,"lifecycle_failures":1,"claim_strength_violations":0,"qualitative_findings":["The lifecycle case loses an explicit clean-state contract, which weakens closeout hygiene more than startup routing.","The read-only startup evidence still exists through `lifecycle/init.sh` and `state/session-handoff.md`, so the damage is localized.","No broader state or scope regression is visible in the archived evidence slice."],"conclusion":"Moderate impact localized to lifecycle closeout; the benchmark slice still runs, but one lifecycle case loses clean-state support."},{"variant_id":"remove_evaluator_rubric","removed_component":"verification/evaluator-rubric.md","cases_executed":5,"pass":4,"partial":1,"fail":0,"not_evaluated":0,"state_failures":0,"verification_failures":1,"scope_creep_count":0,"lifecycle_failures":0,"claim_strength_violations":0,"qualitative_findings":["The verification-before-completion case is the most sensitive to this removal because the rubric is the explicit completion gate.","The actor output can still point at `verification/claim_strength_checklist.json`, but the authoritative verification contract is missing.","This weakens completion gating without implying any production-grade evidence."],"conclusion":"Moderate impact concentrated in verification gating; the affected case still has a fallback signal, but the rubric removal is material."},{"variant_id":"remove_progress","removed_component":"state/progress.md","cases_executed":5,"pass":4,"partial":1,"fail":0,"not_evaluated":0,"state_failures":1,"verification_failures":0,"scope_creep_count":0,"lifecycle_failures":0,"claim_strength_violations":0,"qualitative_findings":["The resume path loses the explicit progress ledger, so blocker visibility and handoff deltas become less complete.","`state/session-handoff.md` still carries the restart surface, so the degradation is continuity-related rather than catastrophic.","The remaining shared-harness cases do not show collateral scope or verification regressions."],"conclusion":"Moderate impact on session continuity; one state case degrades because progress is the explicit carry-forward surface."},{"variant_id":"remove_scope_policy","removed_component":"autonomous/07_scope/SCOPE_POLICY.md","cases_executed":5,"pass":4,"partial":1,"fail":0,"not_evaluated":0,"state_failures":0,"verification_failures":0,"scope_creep_count":1,"lifecycle_failures":0,"claim_strength_violations":0,"qualitative_findings":["The scope case loses the explicit BE-only rule, which is the main boundary against unrelated v35 refactors.","`state/feature_list.json` still gives some structure, but it is not a full substitute for the scope policy.","The evidence slice indicates elevated scope-creep risk rather than an observed destructive refactor."],"conclusion":"Moderate impact concentrated in scope control; the missing policy is material even though no out-of-bounds rewrite is observed."},{"variant_id":"remove_session_handoff","removed_component":"state/session-handoff.md","cases_executed":5,"pass":3,"partial":2,"fail":0,"not_evaluated":0,"state_failures":2,"verification_failures":0,"scope_creep_count":0,"lifecycle_failures":0,"claim_strength_violations":0,"qualitative_findings":["Two benchmark cases rely on the session handoff as the explicit restart packet, so removing it degrades resumability across the 